{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785012159,"nonce":"LgnV4QvxoTT4YSZ0WMrUP1U3woc=","message":"VERIFIED against a real Forgejo (codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo:16.0.1). Branch integrate/open-issues-2026-07-26.\n\njust forgejo-verify — exit 0:\n  live::list_accessible_repos_walks_past_the_first_page                  PASS\n  live::a_registered_hook_delivers_a_signed_push_we_can_normalize        PASS\n  forgejo_onboarding::a_real_forgejo_repo_onboards_and_its_push_becomes_a_run  PASS\n\nGate: SCARAB_TEST_FORGEJO=1 (plus SCARAB_E2E=1 for the onboarding leg), mirroring SCARAB_TEST_KUBE; both skip loudly, CI runs neither. Stack lives in deploy/local-forgejo/ (throwaway SQLite Forgejo, seeded with 57 repos so pagination is really exercised).\n\nAcceptance:\n- [x] connection create, available-repos, bind, register_webhook all succeed against a real Forgejo\n- [x] a real push produces a signed delivery /webhooks/forgejo accepts and turns into a Run (hook confirmed carrying the secret; hook URL confirmed on the wire)\n- [x] shape mismatches fixed with unit tests pinning the real shape\n- [x] gated so CI does not require a Forgejo\n\nFOUR real defects the tier caught — the point of the exercise:\n\n1. Hook.url is top-level while Hook.config is deprecated; our idempotency check read only config.url, so re-registration created DUPLICATE hooks. (from Forgejo swagger v16, fixed + unit test)\n2. Paging stopped on a SHORT page rather than an empty one — Forgejo produces short pages whenever MAX_RESPONSE_ITEMS is below our page size, so the pick-list silently truncated. (fixed + unit test)\n3. SCARAB_PUBLIC_URL was silently ignored for webhook registration (fc66215). AppState.public_url was only ever assigned by with_oauth_login, so with login disabled every hook Scarab registered pointed at the hardcoded http://localhost:8080 — registration reporting success while no delivery could ever arrive. This is the register_webhook config.secret bug`s twin and it affected Helm deployments too, not just this tier. with_oauth_login lost the parameter entirely so it cannot be re-coupled; try_register_webhook now warns when a callback resolves to loopback.\n4. deploy/local-proc/up.sh could succeed against a server it did not start (01d5a74). A stale orphan on 8080 made the tier drive the OLD binary for two full false-red runs — and could as easily have produced a false GREEN, which would have made this whole tier worthless as evidence. up.sh now claims the port first and refuses; it also proves the child is alive before declaring the stack up. Guard verified by putting a foreign listener on 8080: exit 1 with an actionable message.\n\nAlso fixed: the compose DB path (/data/forgejo is outside the only subtree the image entrypoint chowns, so Forgejo died in a DB-init retry loop before binding), and the scenario is now re-runnable — it reclaims a connection left by an earlier run (single-owner precedence correctly 409s) and requires a NEW Run id, since durable Runs from a previous invocation would otherwise satisfy the poll and read green.\n\nSTILL UNPROVEN: contract_live.rs is excluded from the recipe (its list_dir_at_ref fixture uses dir: \"\" and may 404, reddening the tier for an unrelated reason) — see deploy/local-forgejo/README.md for the one-liner to run it.","files":null}]}